framework fidelity: covariant LinearLayout params, addView with the inflated params, and what a tablet-sized Instagram needed

LinearLayout.generateLayoutParams(AttributeSet) returns LinearLayout.LayoutParams,
as in AOSP (TableLayout / TableRow / RadioGroup follow with their own). An app
subclass compiled against the SDK calls super by the descriptor that returns
LinearLayout$LayoutParams; with only the ViewGroup$LayoutParams one that was a
NoSuchMethodError -- Instagram 455: IgLinearLayout.generateLayoutParams, 377
times per launch, each falling back to parameters the app's override never saw.
After: 0.

LayoutInflater hands the generated params to addView(view, params) with the view
carrying none, as rInflate does, instead of setLayoutParams + addView(view). A
parent that re-parents its child sees the difference: SlidingPaneLayout wraps
the detail pane with `new TouchBlocker(child)` -> addView(child), which on a
device gives a params-less child MATCH_PARENT and here inherited the pane's own
layout_width (300dp). Measured on Instagram's tablet inbox: the "Suas mensagens"
panel was 300px wide at the left edge of an 816px pane; after, it is centred.
MACAPK_INFLATE_ADDVIEW_PARAMS=0 restores the old call.

ViewStub, APP QUIRK (Instagram): when the large-screen rail's stub
(ls_vertical_nav_bar_stub) inflates, the phone tab bar and its 1px separator
(tab_bar, tab_bar_shadow) go GONE. They stay in the main layout on a large
screen, the app's own updater returns early while the rail is up, and the empty
bar's separator was drawn across the content 48px above the bottom of the
window. What removes it on a device was not found (MACAPK_TRACE_SETVIS on both
ids: no call besides the inflater's background). MACAPK_QUIRK_RAIL_TABBAR=0
turns the quirk off.

VMRuntime.setTargetHeapUtilization / getTargetHeapUtilization exist (a
NoSuchMethodError once per launch). View: MACAPK_TRACE_SETVIS=<id> logs every
setVisibility / setAlpha / setTranslationY / setBackground* on that view and who
asked.

